{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEach plan-review pass re-sends the full plan with no cross-pass cache reuse, and the anthropic cache breakpoint sits on the WHOLE system block (`anthropic_cache_instructions=True`, src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:39-52), so only byte-identical system prompts share a cache entry. Today the two passes render through different paths with no shared plan-bearing prefix: Pass-1 finder builds its system prompt via `passes._resolve_system` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:276-292) = `_SHARED_PREAMBLE` (passes.py:264) + the rendered finder template, whose `{{plan}}` sits at the template END (src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_finder.md:30-31, no volatile marker); Pass-2 verify runs via the workflow `RunnerAgentStep` (src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py:245) → `prompts.resolve_prompt_cached` (src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:380-405), which splits at the `<!--volatile-->` marker (plan_review_verifier.md:173 / plan_review_verifier_agentic.md:181 — the agentic arm is the primary production path) and routes the rendered `{{plan}}` into the USER message; the per-run finding listing arrives separately as `base_instructions` (the `instructions` output of `plan_review_verify_inputs`, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:363-395). So the Pass-2 system prompt never contains the plan, and no plan-bearing prefix is shared across passes. The codebase's cache floor is `CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:49 — the Opus 4.8 minimum used by the warmup logic at pass1.py:222,496), which this change adopts as its threshold (NOT the older 1024 figure). Separately, incremental-depth BLOCK loops need an exhaustiveness directive in the shared reviewing stance.\n\n## Approach\nByte identity by construction, single-sourced in code — no template gains a variable that any renderer cannot supply.\n(1) **`prompts.py` gains the single source**: a module constant `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE` (the text of `passes._SHARED_PREAMBLE`, moved verbatim, PLUS one new bullet — the exhaustiveness directive: \"When surfacing findings, enumerate EVERY independent defect you find in THIS run; do not defer deeper or additional findings to a later review round.\") and `shared_plan_prefix(plan: str) -> str` returning `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE + \"# Plan under review (verbatim, whole)\\n\" + plan + \"\\n\\n\"`. Placement rationale: prompts.py already owns the cache-prefix seam (`VOLATILE_MARKER`/`split_volatile`/`resolve_prompt_cached`, prompts.py:349-405) and stays stdlib-only; passes.py is at 798 LOC against the 800 hard cap and cannot absorb the builder, and the module-size policy forbids a new <100-LOC leaf module.\n(2) **Pass-1 rule, exact**: `passes._SHARED_PREAMBLE` is DELETED. `_resolve_system(prompt_id, plan, cfg)` renders the template with variables `{\"plan\": plan, \"shared_prefix\": prompts.shared_plan_prefix(plan)}` (strict rendering only requires USED variables — prompts.py:321-330 — so the superset is harmless to every template), then returns `prompts.shared_plan_prefix(plan) + strip_volatile_marker(rendered)` when `prompt_id == PASS_FINDER`, else `prompts.SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE + strip_volatile_marker(rendered)` (byte-equal to today's behavior for container/ISF/completion/coach, modulo the added directive bullet). `plan_review_finder.md` drops its trailing \"# Plan under review …\\n{{plan}}\" block (stance-only template; no marker added — the prefix boundary is explicit in code). Container/ISF/completion/coach templates are NOT restructured (their `{{plan}}` stays at the template bottom; separate prompt_ids and cache entries). The directive lives in the preamble, so it reaches EVERY Pass-1 request (finder chunks, container, ISF) and, by byte-identity, the verifier prefix too, where its \"when surfacing findings\" phrasing is inert.\n(3) **Verifier templates**: both `plan_review_verifier.md` and `plan_review_verifier_agentic.md` begin their body with a `{{shared_prefix}}` line followed by the existing stance text unchanged, and DELETE the trailing `<!--volatile-->` + \"# Plan under review …\\n{{plan}}\" block entirely. With no marker left, `split_volatile` takes its no-marker path (prompts.py:361-363): the WHOLE rendered template is the stable system prompt and `instructions` = `base_instructions` (the per-chunk finding listing stays user-turn — unchanged mechanism). Neither verifier declares front-matter `variables:`, so the contract change is exactly \"used var `plan` → used var `shared_prefix`\" under the legacy strict path; no parity-gate front-matter edit is needed.\n(4) **How `shared_prefix` reaches the live variable map — the exact seam**: `plan_review_verify_inputs` (workflow_ops.py:363) additionally returns `\"shared_prefix\": prompts.shared_plan_prefix(pctx.plan_text)`; `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verify_inputs_output.schema.json` (currently `additionalProperties: false`) gains the `shared_prefix` string property (required); and BOTH verify steps in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml` (the agentic arm's `verify` at line ~177 and the single-turn arm's at line ~288) replace `plan: ${{ steps.verify_inputs.outputs.plan }}` with `shared_prefix: ${{ steps.verify_inputs.outputs.shared_prefix }}` in their `with:` blocks. `runs.py` needs NO edit: `RunnerAgentStep` already merges every string-valued `with:` input into the render variables (runs.py:204-207), so `shared_prefix` flows to `resolve_prompt_cached` through the existing generic mechanism — runs.py is an AUDITED consumer with zero changes.\n(5) **Every renderer of the verifier templates, enumerated**: (a) `RunnerAgentStep` — covered by (4); (b) `fidelity_spot_eval.py` — `plan-review-verifier` is REMOVED from `RELOCATED_PROMPTS` (fidelity_spot_eval.py:46-54, comment updated): the verifiers no longer carry the split marker so they are no longer \"relocated\" prompts, `test_relocated_prompts_all_carry_the_split_marker` (tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py) then passes over the remaining entries, and no committed corpus renders a verifier (`RELOCATED_PROMPTS`/`relocation_spot_eval` have no consumers outside the module + that test; the unit-test corpus uses `completion-verifier` only), so `_relocation_requests` never sees `{{shared_prefix}}` and needs no change; (c) `passes._resolve_system` — supplies both variables per (2) (live code never calls it with the verifier ids; the bespoke pass2 was retired in epic solid-timer-unison WS1); (d) direct test renderers, each updated to supply `shared_prefix` (or drop `plan`): tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py (remove the two verifier ids from `_MARKED_PROMPTS`; repoint `test_bespoke_plan_review_path_strips_marker_and_keeps_plan_in_system` at the finder prefix invariant), tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_live_plumbing.py (`test_runner_agent_step_resolves_plan_for_verify`), tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_verify_recovery.py (`_verify_ctx` inputs), tests/unit/test_llm_temperature.py (the `plan-review-verifier` StepContext inputs), tests/external/test_review_kernel_rules_live.py:74-77 (supply `shared_prefix=prompts.shared_plan_prefix(context)`). The `plan-review-verifier.eval.yaml` standing spec references the prompt id but never renders the template offline (tests/unit/test_plan_review_evals.py validates spec structure only). (e) CONTRIBUTING.md:620 names `_SHARED_PREAMBLE` — updated to `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE`/`shared_plan_prefix` in prompts.py.\n(6) **No verdict/TTL change**: verify stays per-chunk with merge-by-index; temperature/budget `with:` inputs untouched; no TTL change. Alternatives rejected: raising cache TTL to 1h (pass gaps of 50-100ms never approach the 5-minute refresh-on-hit window; revise loops change the prefix bytes, so the 2x write premium buys nothing); padding the preamble itself past the 4096-token floor without moving the plan (a >4096-token boilerplate preamble adds that many tokens of pure overhead to every call, while the plan bytes are ALREADY sent per pass — making them the cached prefix costs nothing extra).\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py (SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE + shared_plan_prefix), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py (delete _SHARED_PREAMBLE; _resolve_system branch + variables), src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_finder.md (drop trailing plan block), src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md and plan_review_verifier_agentic.md ({{shared_prefix}} head; delete volatile tail), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py (verify_inputs emits shared_prefix), src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verify_inputs_output.schema.json (add shared_prefix), src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml (both verify `with:` blocks), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py (RELOCATED_PROMPTS minus plan-review-verifier), CONTRIBUTING.md (stale symbol reference), tests/unit/workflow/test_shared_prefix.py (new), tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_live_plumbing.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_verify_recovery.py, tests/unit/test_llm_temperature.py, tests/external/test_review_kernel_rules_live.py (updated renderers). Audited, no change: src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py (generic string `with:`-merge at runs.py:204-207 already carries shared_prefix).\n\n## Testing\nNew tests/unit/workflow/test_shared_prefix.py (offline, FakeRunner/no model), against a named in-file fixture plan `FIXTURE_PLAN` built programmatically to exceed the cache floor (the test_pass1_warmup.py:88 approach): (1) `passes._resolve_system(passes.PASS_FINDER, FIXTURE_PLAN, cfg)` and the `resolve_prompt_cached` stable segment of BOTH verifier prompts (rendered with `shared_prefix=prompts.shared_plan_prefix(FIXTURE_PLAN)`) each `startswith(prompts.shared_plan_prefix(FIXTURE_PLAN))` byte-for-byte, and that prefix contains the full plan text; (2) `det_floor.est_tokens(shared_plan_prefix(FIXTURE_PLAN)) >= pass1.CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (the imported constant — currently 4096 — so a future floor change re-verifies automatically); (3) the exhaustiveness directive is in `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE` and hence in `_resolve_system` output for PASS_FINDER, PASS_CONTAINER, and PASS_ISF (every Pass-1 entry point); (4) a sentinel finding listing passed as `base_instructions` appears in the returned `instructions` and NOT in the stable system segment, for both verifiers; (5) `not hasattr(passes, \"_SHARED_PREAMBLE\")`; (6) rendering the verifier prompts through `RunnerAgentStep` with a StepContext whose inputs mirror the yaml `with:` (findings/instructions/shared_prefix) succeeds. Updated existing tests as enumerated in Approach (5d). Regression: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/` then the full `tests/unit` suite; tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py (full-yaml fixture runs) passes UNMODIFIED — verdict behavior unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] For the named fixture plan, the Pass-1 finder system prompt and the rendered stable segments of BOTH verifier prompts each begin byte-for-byte with `prompts.shared_plan_prefix(plan)`, which contains the full plan material (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_shared_prefix.py`).\n- [ ] `det_floor.est_tokens(shared_plan_prefix(FIXTURE_PLAN))` >= `pass1.CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (asserted against the imported constant, currently 4096 — pass1.py:49) (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_shared_prefix.py`).\n- [ ] The reviewing-stance preamble text exists ONCE, as `prompts.SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE`, and `passes._SHARED_PREAMBLE` is removed (checked: unit test asserting `not hasattr(passes, \"_SHARED_PREAMBLE\")` and that `_resolve_system` output for a non-restructured pass starts with `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE`).\n- [ ] The exhaustiveness directive is a bullet of `SHARED_STANCE_PREAMBLE` and present in the `_resolve_system` system prompt of every Pass-1 entry point (PASS_FINDER, PASS_CONTAINER, PASS_ISF) (checked: unit test in test_shared_prefix.py).\n- [ ] The per-run finding listing remains user-turn (`base_instructions` → `instructions`) and is absent from every rendered stable system segment (checked: unit test in test_shared_prefix.py).\n- [ ] `plan-review-verifier` is removed from `RELOCATED_PROMPTS` and every remaining entry still carries the volatile marker (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py::test_relocated_prompts_all_carry_the_split_marker` with the updated tuple).\n- [ ] Both plan-review.yaml verify steps supply `shared_prefix` from `verify_inputs` outputs and the live render path resolves without PromptError (checked: unit test rendering via RunnerAgentStep with yaml-shaped inputs; `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py` full-yaml runs).\n- [ ] Review verdict behavior on the existing workflow fixtures is unchanged (checked: tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py passes unmodified)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785435787511938001,"uuid":"c3e2ca6d-60a4-4e0d-b3e2-fa8f95987869"}